  "learn": "On Unix, any file whose name starts with a dot is **hidden**: `ls` and the `*` glob skip it by default.\n`ls -a` (all) or `ls -A` (all except `.` and `..`) reveal them. Config files love to hide this way:\n`.bashrc`, `.gitignore`, `.ssh/`. A glob that starts with a literal dot, like `.t*`, can match them.",
