  "order": 25,
  "dir": "/var/challenges/caps_lock",
  "title": "CAPS LOCK",
  "story": "The CEO wants the outage report in ALL CAPS \"so people understand it was serious\".\nYou have been told this is non-negotiable.",
  "description": "Print the contents of `report.txt` converted to uppercase. Everything that isn't a\nlowercase letter (digits, punctuation, spaces, indentation) must stay exactly as it is.",
  "hints": [
   "There's a command that **tr**anslates characters from one set into another.",
   "Sets can be ranges: `tr 'a-z' 'A-Z'`. It only reads standard input, so use `<` or a pipe."
  ],
  "learn": "`tr SET1 SET2` replaces each character in SET1 with the character at the same position in SET2.\nIt only reads standard input. Ranges (`a-z`) and classes (`[:lower:]`, `[:digit:]`, `[:space:]`)\nare supported, `-d` deletes characters and `-s` squeezes repeats.",
