  "learn": "`jq` reads JSON and runs a filter program over it. Filters chain with `|`: `.[]` streams array\nelements, `.field` extracts a key, `select(cond)` keeps elements where cond is true, and\n`map(f)` applies a filter to every element of an array. By default jq prints JSON (strings in\nquotes); `-r` prints raw text, which is what other shell tools want.",
