  "dir": "/var/challenges/json_to_csv",
  "title": "JSON to CSV",
  "story": "The finance team does not speak JSON. They speak spreadsheet, fluently and loudly.\nTranslate `orders.json` before the next quarterly meeting.",
  "description": "`orders.json` is an array of orders. Print a CSV with a header row followed by one row per\norder (in file order) containing the fields `id`, `customer` and `total`.\n\nFormat everything exactly like jq's `@csv` does: strings in double quotes, numbers bare.\nThe header row is therefore `\"id\",\"customer\",\"total\"` and a data row looks like `1001,\"Ada Bytes\",59.99`.",
  "hints": [
   "jq can build an array from fields: `[.id, .customer, .total]`. Pipe an array into `@csv`.",
   "Use `-r` and emit the header array first: `[\"id\",\"customer\",\"total\"], (.[] | [...]) | @csv`."
  ],
  "learn": "jq's format strings turn arrays into text: `@csv` (quoted CSV), `@tsv` (tab-separated),\n`@json`, `@base64` and more. The comma operator emits several results in sequence, so\n`header, (rows)` prints the header first. `-r` is required; otherwise each CSV line would be\nprinted as a JSON string.",
  "solutions": [
   {
    "cmd": "jq -r '[\"id\", \"customer\", \"total\"], (.[] | [.id, .customer, .total]) | @csv' orders.json",
    "note": "Reference solution"
   },
   {
    "cmd": "echo '\"id\",\"customer\",\"total\"'; jq -r '.[] | [.id, .customer, .total] | @csv' orders.json",
    "note": "Hand-write the header, let jq do the rows."
   },
   {
    "cmd": "jq -r '[\"id\", \"customer\", \"total\"] as $k | $k, (.[] | [.[$k[]]]) | @csv' orders.json",
    "note": "Store the header in `$k` and use it to look up the fields too. Very DRY."
   },
   {
    "cmd": "{ echo '\"id\",\"customer\",\"total\"'; jq -r '.[] | \"\\(.id),\\\"\\(.customer)\\\",\\(.total)\"' orders.json; }",
    "note": "String interpolation with `\\(...)`. Works because no customer name contains a quote."
   }
  ],
  "timeLimit": 240,
  "tags": [
   "jq",
   "json",
   "csv"
  ],
