  "learn": "Globs are patterns that bash expands into matching file names: `*` matches any run of\ncharacters (even none), `?` exactly one, and `[Hh]` one character from the set. They're\ncase-sensitive, so `[Hh]ippolyta*` covers both spellings, while the lazier `[Hh]ippo*` would also\ndrag in the hippo's bathtub. Names with spaces or apostrophes are no problem: each match reaches\nthe command as one intact argument. `shopt -s nocaseglob` makes globs ignore case altogether.",
