   "`\\b` marks a word boundary, so `\\btoad\\b` leaves `toadstool` alone. Two substitutions can share one sed: separate them with `;`.",
   "`sed 's/\\btoad\\b/gummy frog/g; s/\\bToad\\b/Gummy frog/g' recipe.txt`"
