  "dir": "/var/challenges/carving_station",
  "title": "Carving Station",
  "story": "Jack O'Latency supervises the carving station, which is a little awkward for him.\nThe pumpkins in the patch are scooped and waiting. Time to give them faces.",
  "description": "Carve every pumpkin in `patch/`: rename each file in `patch/` whose name ends in `.pumpkin`\nso that it ends in `.jack` instead (`patch/lumpy.pumpkin` becomes `patch/lumpy.jack`).\nSome names contain spaces.\n\nKeep the contents, leave every other file alone, and do **not** carve `prize.pumpkin`\n(outside the patch): it's entered in the giant gourd contest.",
  "hints": [
   "`mv old new` renames one file. For a whole patch, loop: `for f in patch/*.pumpkin; do ...; done`.",
   "`${f%.pumpkin}` is `$f` with the `.pumpkin` ending removed. Add `.jack`, and put double quotes around both names so the spaces survive.",
   "`for f in patch/*.pumpkin; do mv \"$f\" \"${f%.pumpkin}.jack\"; done`"
  ],
  "learn": "Bulk renames are loops: walk a glob, build each new name with parameter expansion, `mv`.\n`${f%suffix}` removes a suffix, `${f#prefix}` removes a prefix and `${f/%old/new}` replaces at\nthe end. Always double-quote `\"$f\"`: unquoted, `big grin.pumpkin` falls apart into two\narguments. The Perl `rename` tool applies a regex to many names at once, and `basename f .ext`\nstrips both the folder and an extension.",
  "solutions": [
   {
    "cmd": "for f in patch/*.pumpkin; do mv \"$f\" \"${f%.pumpkin}.jack\"; done",
    "note": "Reference solution"
   },
   {
    "cmd": "rename 's/\\.pumpkin$/.jack/' patch/*.pumpkin",
    "note": "The Perl-flavoured `rename` carves with a regex: one command, the whole patch."
   },
   {
    "cmd": "cd patch && for f in *.pumpkin; do mv -- \"$f\" \"${f%.*}.jack\"; done",
    "note": "Step into the patch first. `${f%.*}` drops the last extension, whatever it is."
   },
   {
    "cmd": "find patch -name '*.pumpkin' -exec sh -c 'mv \"$1\" \"${1%.pumpkin}.jack\"' _ {} \\;",
    "note": "find hands each pumpkin to a tiny shell script as `$1`. Spaces can't hurt it."
   },
   {
    "cmd": "ls patch/*.pumpkin | while IFS= read -r f; do mv \"$f\" \"${f/%.pumpkin/.jack}\"; done",
    "note": "One name per line into a read loop; `${f/%old/new}` replaces only at the very end."
   },
   {
    "cmd": "for f in patch/*.pumpkin; do mv \"$f\" \"patch/$(basename \"$f\" .pumpkin).jack\"; done",
    "note": "`basename name .pumpkin` strips the folder and the suffix; glue the folder back on."
   }
  ],
  "timeLimit": 180,
  "tags": [
   "mv",
   "loops",
   "parameter-expansion",
   "rename"
  ],
