  "learn": "`sort` reads every line, puts them in order and prints the result; the file itself is not\nchanged (use `sort -o file file` or a redirect to save it). Lines are compared character by\ncharacter, which is why `Mabel` comes before `Mae` (`b` beats `e`). Handy flags: `-r` reverses,\n`-f` ignores case, `-n` sorts numbers by value and `-u` drops duplicate lines.",
